[
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-01",
    "question": "<p><strong>M</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}x&amp;x-2\\\\3x-6&amp;4x-11\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>\nGiven that the matrix <strong>M</strong> is singular, find the possible values of <em>x</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>For a two-by-two matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\bigl(\\begin{smallmatrix}a&amp;b\\\\c&amp;d\\end{smallmatrix}\\bigr)\"></span>, singularity is the condition <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ad=bc\"></span>. Here the off-diagonal product is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(x-2)^2\"></span>, so its entire expansion must be subtracted. Substituting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\"></span> into the determinant checks both roots.</p>",
      "<p>A singular matrix has determinant zero. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x(4x-11)-(x-2)(3x-6)=0\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Expanding gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2-11x-(3x^2-12x+12)=x^2+x-12=0\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+4)(x-3)=0\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-4\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 4 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-01-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q1, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-02",
    "question": "<p><strong><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-1\\\\4&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{P}=\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;6\\\\11&amp;-8\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></strong></p><p>(<em>a</em>) Find <strong>A</strong><sup>–1</sup>\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span>\nThe transformation represented by the matrix <strong>B</strong> followed by the transformation represented\nby the matrix <strong>A</strong> is equivalent to the transformation represented by the matrix <strong>P</strong>.</p><p>(<em>b</em>) Find <strong>B</strong>, giving your answer in its simplest form.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>A column vector encounters the rightmost matrix first. This gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=P\"></span>, so premultiply by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^{-1}\"></span> to cancel the adjacent <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. Checking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> times the first column of your answer gives the first column of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det A=2(3)-(-1)(4)=10\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^{-1}=\\tfrac1{10}\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\-4&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) Applying <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> first gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=P\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=A^{-1}P\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=\\frac1{10}\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1\\\\-4&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;6\\\\11&amp;-8\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1\\\\1&amp;-4\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 5 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-02-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q2, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-03",
    "question": "<p>(i) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}2k+1&amp;k\\\\-3&amp;-5\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , where <em>k</em> is a constant\nGiven that <strong>B</strong> = <strong>A</strong> + 3<strong>I</strong>\nwhere <strong>I</strong> is the 2 × 2 identity matrix, find</p><p>(<em>a</em>) <strong>B</strong> in terms of <em>k</em>,\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) the value of <em>k</em> for which <strong>B</strong> is singular.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span>\n(ii) Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{C}=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-3\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , <strong>D</strong> = (2 –1 5)\nand <strong>E</strong> = <strong>CD</strong>\nfind <strong>E</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Adding <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3I\"></span> changes each diagonal entry by three and leaves the off-diagonal entries alone. In the outer product a column of three entries multiplies a row of three entries, so the result has nine entries. Each row is a multiple of the same row vector.</p>",
      "<p>(i)(a) Add 3 to each diagonal entry. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B=\\begin{pmatrix}2k+4&amp;k\\\\-3&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det B=-2(2k+4)+3k=0\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=-8\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) Each row of the product is the corresponding entry of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> times <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span>.</p>",
      "<div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"E=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;-2&amp;10\\\\-6&amp;3&amp;-15\\\\8&amp;-4&amp;20\\end{pmatrix}.\"></div>",
      "<p><small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-03-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q3, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-04",
    "question": "<p>(<em>a</em>) Given that <strong>A</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;1&amp;3\\\\4&amp;5&amp;5\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> and <strong>B = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1\\\\1&amp;2\\\\0&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> ,</strong>\nfind <strong>AB</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) Given that <strong>C</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}3&amp;2\\\\8&amp;6\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> and <strong>D =</strong> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}5&amp;2k\\\\4&amp;k\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , where <em>k</em> is a constant\nand <strong>E</strong> = <strong>C</strong> + <strong>D</strong>,\nfind the value of <em>k</em> for which <strong>E</strong> has no inverse.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>To calculate an entry of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span>, pair the entries of one row of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> with the matching entries of a column of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>, then add. For the second calculation zero determinant means the two rows of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E\"></span> are proportional. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=3/2\"></span>, the second row is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3/2\"></span> times the first.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Use row-by-column products: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=\\begin{pmatrix}3+1&amp;3+2-3\\\\4+5&amp;4+10-5\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;2\\\\9&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E=\\begin{pmatrix}8&amp;2+2k\\\\12&amp;6+k\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>For no inverse, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8(6+k)-12(2+2k)=0\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24-16k=0\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=3/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-04-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q4, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-05",
    "question": "<p><strong>A</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\5&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , <strong>B = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}-3&amp;-1\\\\5&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></strong></p><p>(<em>a</em>) Find <strong>AB</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span>\nGiven that <strong>C</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) describe fully the geometrical transformation represented by <strong>C</strong>,\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>c</em>) write down <strong>C</strong><sup>100</sup>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Apply the transformation to the general point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x,y)\"></span>. Changing the sign of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> keeps the entire <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis fixed and exchanges its two sides. Applying that reflection twice returns every point to its start, so an even power acts as the identity.</p>",
      "<p>(a) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=\\begin{pmatrix}-6&amp;-2\\\\-15+15&amp;-5+6\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-6&amp;-2\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[3]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(x,y)^{\\mathsf T}=(-x,y)^{\\mathsf T}\"></span>, a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C^2=I\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C^{100}=I\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 6 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-05-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q5, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-06",
    "question": "<p>(<em>a</em>) Given that <strong>A</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;\\sqrt2\\\\\\sqrt2&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> ,\n(i) find <strong>A</strong><sup>2</sup>,\n(ii) describe fully the geometrical transformation represented by <strong>A</strong><sup>2</sup>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) Given that <strong>B</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> ,\ndescribe fully the geometrical transformation represented by <strong>B</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>c</em>) Given that <strong>C</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}k+1&amp;12\\\\k&amp;9\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> ,\nwhere <em>k</em> is a constant, find the value of <em>k</em> for which the matrix <strong>C</strong> is singular.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>An off-diagonal zero in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^2\"></span> results from two equal terms with opposite signs. The diagonal <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3I\"></span> sends every position vector to three times itself. In the reflection part, points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(t,-t)\"></span> stay fixed, which identifies the mirror line.</p>",
      "<p>(a)(i) Multiplication gives diagonal terms <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+2=3\"></span> and off-diagonal terms <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2-\\sqrt2=0\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A^2=3I\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small>\n(ii) This is an enlargement of scale factor 3 about the origin. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x,y)\\mapsto(-y,-x)\"></span> is a reflection in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) For singularity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9(k+1)-12k=0\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=3\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 9 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-06-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q6, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-07",
    "question": "<p>(i) Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\\\3&amp;-1\\\\4&amp;5\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{B}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-1&amp;4\\\\1&amp;3&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> ,</p><p>(<em>a</em>) find <strong>AB</strong>.</p><p>(<em>b</em>) Explain why <strong>AB</strong> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ne\"></span> <strong>BA</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span>\n(ii) Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{C}=\\begin{pmatrix}2k&amp;-2\\\\3&amp;k\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , where <em>k</em> is a real number\nfind <strong>C</strong><sup>–1</sup>, giving your answer in terms of <em>k</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>The inner dimensions in the matrix product tell you how many products to add for each entry. Reversing the order also reverses which outer dimensions survive. For the inverse, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2k^2+6\\ge6\"></span> ensures the division is valid at every real <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(i)(a) Multiply each row of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> by each column of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span>:</p>",
      "<div class=\"equation\" data-display=\"true\" data-math=\"AB=\\begin{pmatrix}2+2&amp;-1+6&amp;4+2\\\\6-1&amp;-3-3&amp;12-1\\\\8+5&amp;-4+15&amp;16+5\\end{pmatrix}\n=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;5&amp;6\\\\5&amp;-6&amp;11\\\\13&amp;11&amp;21\\end{pmatrix}.\"></div>",
      "<p><small class=\"step-credit\">[3]</small>\n(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB\"></span> has order <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\times3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BA\"></span> has order <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det C=2k^2+6\"></span> is positive for all real <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C^{-1}=\\frac1{2k^2+6}\\begin{pmatrix}k&amp;2\\\\-3&amp;2k\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 7 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-07-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q7, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-08",
    "question": "<p>The transformation <em>U</em>, represented by the 2 × 2 matrix <strong>P</strong>, is a rotation through 90° anticlockwise about the origin.</p><p>(<em>a</em>) Write down the matrix <strong>P</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span>\nThe transformation <em>V</em>, represented by the 2 × 2 matrix <strong>Q</strong>, is a reflection in the line <em>y</em> = −<em>x</em>.</p><p>(<em>b</em>) Write down the matrix <strong>Q</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span>\nGiven that <em>U</em> followed by <em>V</em> is transformation <em>T</em>, which is represented by the matrix <strong>R</strong>,</p><p>(<em>c</em>) express <strong>R</strong> in terms of <strong>P</strong> and <strong>Q</strong>,\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p><p>(<em>d</em>) find the matrix <strong>R</strong>,\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>e</em>) give a full geometrical description of <em>T</em> as a single transformation.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Read the columns as the images of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\"></span>. Applying <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> takes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1)\"></span> and then <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,0)\"></span>. This independently checks the first column of the composite.</p>",
      "<p>(a) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=QP\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(d) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;-1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;0\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(e) This maps <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x,y)\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-x,y)\"></span>, a reflection in the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 7 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-08-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q8, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-09",
    "question": "<p>A right angled triangle <em>T</em> has vertices <em>A</em>(1, 1), <em>B</em>(2, 1) and <em>C</em>(2, 4). When <em>T</em> is transformed by the matrix <strong>P</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , the image is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;\"></span>.</p><p>(<em>a</em>) Find the coordinates of the vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;\"></span>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) Describe fully the transformation represented by <strong>P</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span>\nThe matrices <strong>Q</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;-2\\\\3&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> and <strong>R</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\\\3&amp;4\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> represent two transformations. When <em>T</em> is transformed by the matrix <strong>QR</strong>, the image is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;&#x27;\"></span>.</p><p>(<em>c</em>) Find <strong>QR</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>d</em>) Find the determinant of <strong>QR</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>(<em>e</em>) Using your answer to part (<em>d</em>), find the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T&#x27;&#x27;\"></span>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Swapping coordinates fixes the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\"></span>, which identifies the reflection. The determinant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\"></span> later records two separate facts: the image has reversed orientation and areas have been multiplied by four. Use its absolute value for the triangular area.</p>",
      "<p>(a) The matrix swaps the two coordinates, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A&#x27;=(1,1),\\ B&#x27;=(1,2),\\ C&#x27;=(4,2)\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) It is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"QR=\\begin{pmatrix}4-6&amp;8-8\\\\3-3&amp;6-4\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}-2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(d) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det(QR)=(-2)(2)-0=-4\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(e) The original triangle has area <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tfrac12(1)(3)=3/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Use the absolute determinant as the area multiplier: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\times3/2=6\"></span> square units. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 11 marks.</p>",
