    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-10",
    "question": "<p>(i)\n<strong><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}p&amp;2\\\\3&amp;p\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{B}=\\begin{pmatrix}-5&amp;4\\\\6&amp;-5\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></strong>\nwhere <em>p</em> is a constant.</p><p>(<em>a</em>) Find, in terms of <em>p</em>, the matrix <strong>AB</strong>\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span>\nGiven that\n<strong>AB +</strong> 2<strong>A =</strong> <em>k</em><strong>I</strong>\nwhere <em>k</em> is a constant and <strong>I</strong> is the 2 × 2 identity matrix,</p><p>(<em>b</em>) find the value of <em>p</em> and the value of <em>k</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span>\n(ii)\n<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{M}=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;-9\\\\1&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , where <em>a</em> is a real constant\nTriangle <em>T</em> has an area of 15 square units.\nTriangle <em>T</em> is transformed to the triangle <em>T′</em> by the transformation represented by the\nmatrix <strong>M</strong>.\nGiven that the area of triangle <em>T′</em> is 270 square units, find the possible values\nof <em>a</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>A scalar multiple of the identity has equal diagonal entries and two zero off-diagonal entries. Both equations for the off-diagonal entries should therefore give the same <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>. For the area calculation either determinant sign can give the same area, so both resulting linear equations are needed.</p>",
      "<p>(i)(a) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB=\\begin{pmatrix}-5p+12&amp;4p-10\\\\6p-15&amp;12-5p\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AB+2A=\\begin{pmatrix}12-3p&amp;4p-6\\\\6p-9&amp;12-3p\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Both off-diagonal entries vanish when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=3/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>The equal diagonal entries then give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=15/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(ii) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det M=2a+9\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>The area multiplier is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"270/15=18=|2a+9|\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Solving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2a+9=18\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2a+9=-18\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=9/2,-27/2\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 11 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-10-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q10, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-11",
    "question": "<p><strong>A</strong> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\begin{pmatrix}-4&amp;a\\\\b&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> , where <em>a</em> and <em>b</em> are constants.\nGiven that the matrix <strong>A</strong> maps the point with coordinates (4, 6) onto the point with coordinates (2, −8),</p><p>(<em>a</em>) find the value of <em>a</em> and the value of <em>b</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span>\nA quadrilateral <em>R</em> has area 30 square units.\nIt is transformed into another quadrilateral <em>S</em> by the matrix <strong>A</strong>.\nUsing your values of <em>a</em> and <em>b</em>,</p><p>(<em>b</em>) find the area of quadrilateral <em>S</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Each image coordinate gives its own scalar equation. The first involves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, the second <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, so they can be solved independently. Once these are fixed, the determinant gives the area of the image of one unit square and scales every other area by the same factor.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Multiplying the matrix by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,6)^{\\mathsf T}\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-16+6a=2\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4b-12=-8\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Thus <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a=3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b=1\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det A=(-4)(-2)-3(1)=5\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>The area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|5|\\times30=150\"></span> square units. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 8 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-11-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q11, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-12",
    "question": "<p><strong><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{P}=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&amp;-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt2}&amp;-\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></strong> .</p><p>(<em>a</em>) Describe fully the single geometrical transformation <em>U</em> represented by the matrix <strong>P</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(2)</span>\nThe transformation <em>U</em> maps the point <em>A</em>, with coordinates (<em>p</em>, <em>q</em>), onto the point <em>B</em>, with coordinates (6<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\"></span>, 3<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt2\"></span>).</p><p>(<em>b</em>) Find the value of <em>p</em> and the value of <em>q</em>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span>\nThe transformation <em>V</em>, represented by the 2 × 2 matrix <strong>Q</strong>, is a reflection in the line with equation <em>y</em> = <em>x</em>.</p><p>(<em>c</em>) Write down the matrix <strong>Q</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span>\nThe transformation <em>U</em> followed by the transformation <em>V</em> is the transformation <em>T</em>. The transformation <em>T</em> is represented by the matrix <strong>R</strong>.</p><p>(<em>d</em>) Find the matrix <strong>R</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>(<em>e</em>) Deduce that the transformation <em>T</em> is self-inverse.\n<span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>For an anticlockwise rotation the first column is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta)\"></span>. Its signs place the rotation in quadrant two. For the last part, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R^2=I\"></span> means a second application undoes the first, which is exactly the defining property of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R^{-1}\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) Comparing with the rotation matrix gives a rotation about the origin through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"135^\\circ\"></span> anticlockwise. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) From the image coordinates, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-p-q=12\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p-q=6\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>Solving gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=-3,\\ q=-9\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>(c) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q=\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\\\\1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>(d) Apply <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> first: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R=QP=\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[3]</small></p>",
      "<p>(e) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R^2=\\tfrac12\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;0\\\\0&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}=I\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R^{-1}=R\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
      "<p>Retained exercise: 10 marks.</p>",
      "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/old-spec/rev04-12-ms-01.webp\" alt=\"Source marking table for Session unverified · local Q12, extract 1\" style=\"display:block;margin:auto;height:auto;object-fit:contain;width:100%;max-height:210mm\"></figure>"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "old-spec/rev04-13",
    "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{A}=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;1\\\\-1&amp;0\\end{pmatrix}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle \\mathbf{B}=\\begin{pmatrix}-1&amp;1\\\\0&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>\nGiven that <strong>M</strong> = (<strong>A</strong> + <strong>B</strong>)(2<strong>A</strong> – <strong>B</strong>),</p><p>(<em>a</em>) calculate the matrix <strong>M</strong>,\n<span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></p><p>(<em>b</em>) find the matrix <strong>C</strong> such that <strong>MC</strong> = <strong>A</strong>.\n<span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
    "steps": [
      "<p>Form both brackets before multiplying, since the order affects the cross terms. When solving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"MC=A\"></span>, premultiplying by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M^{-1}\"></span> places the inverse next to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>. A direct check is to multiply the proposed <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span> on the left and recover <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>.</p>",
      "<p>(a) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A+B=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;2\\\\-1&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>, and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2A-B=\\begin{pmatrix}5&amp;1\\\\-2&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[3]</small></p>",
      "<p>Their product in the stated order is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M=\\begin{pmatrix}5-4&amp;1-2\\\\-5-2&amp;-1-1\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;-1\\\\-7&amp;-2\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[3]</small></p>",
      "<p>(b) <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"MC=A\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=M^{-1}A\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>",
      "<p>As <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\det M=-9\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M^{-1}=-\\frac19\\begin{pmatrix}-2&amp;1\\\\7&amp;1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[2]</small></p>",
      "<p>Multiplying gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C=\\frac19\\begin{pmatrix}5&amp;2\\\\-13&amp;-7\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>. <small class=\"step-credit\">[1]</small></p>"
    ],
    "markSchemeSteps": [
